# OWNER REVIEW
# Mrs Marjorie Gander in her garden: the boss (levels/primrose/keys/gander.gd). The Coalition's top saleswoman, Swyne's
# most loyal supporter in public, and in private his best customer.

~ intro
Gander [cold]: You. The consultant. You're not a consultant, are you.
Nim: I gave very good advice.
Gander: You gave away my stock! Every box! Duds! And they LOVED it!
Gander: Do you know what the Councillor pays me for a record year? Do you know what I've ALREADY SPENT?
Gander: Ladies! Guests! Garden party! Mingle!
[narrator] Her guests drift out across the lawns with their teacups, smiling at nothing. Somewhere among the topiary, something honks.

~ bound
Gander: This is MY bench. That is MY sign. I MADE that sign.
Nim: It's a lovely sign.
[narrator] SWYNE FOR DECENCY, in her own careful hand, over Mrs Gander, tied to her own garden bench.
[narrator] In her handbag, the order book. Forty parties this year, and every one of them booked into a councillor's home. Not by chance.
[narrator] And under the order book, folded small: shipping notes. Crates of "literature", due at the Docks.
Gander: The Councillor will hear about this.
Nim: I'm counting on it.
